# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for ChadVis.
#
# STATUS: starter. Nothing is suppressed here yet, deliberately.
#
# Qt is Homebrew qtbase 6.11.1 and is NOT built with sanitizer support -- it has
# zero __tsan_* undefined symbols. That is the usual reason to expect heavy
# toolkit noise, but the measured probes did not show it: a cross-Qt-thread
# round trip produced exactly one report, and it was the genuine race. So this
# file exists to absorb noise that has NOT been seen, not to hide what has.
#
# Add an entry only for a report you have actually reproduced and judged
# benign, and record why in the comment beside it. A suppression with no
# justification is how a real race gets hidden.
#
# Syntax: <report_type>:<substring matched against the symbolized frames>
# Verify:  TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=cmake/tsan.supp ctest --test-dir build-tsan/tests
# Debug:   TSAN_OPTIONS=verbosity=1 ...
#
# --- Qt internals ---------------------------------------------------------
# Candidates in the order they are most likely to appear. NOT enabled: an
# unreproduced suppression is a guess, and a guess that happens to be wrong is
# indistinguishable from a race being hidden.
#   race:QCoreApplication
#   race:QMutex
#
# --- OpenGL / driver (integration_gl_tests only) --------------------------
# Left out of the sanitizer lane entirely; TSan under a GL driver is a known
# source of unreproducible noise. See the CMakeLists ENVIRONMENT block.
#   race:aglCreateContext
#   race:QOpenGLContext
